course: dictionary
lesson: 9142
title: Sneer and the look of unkindness
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A sneer is a mean, mocking smile or tone that shows someone thinks another person is not good enough. You can sneer with your face, your lip or your voice. Sneer can be a verb (a kid sneers) or a noun (a sneer).
explain: «A kid sneers at Jamal, "Your dad's a jailbird!"» The unkind words that follow are your clue. Nobody mocks something they respect, so sneer must mean to make fun of someone in a nasty way. Try it: "A kid makes fun of Jamal" still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: «Ava doesn't sneer; she sets up two seed trays instead.» The word "instead" tells you the opposite. Ava does not mock anyone; she gets on with her own work. The sentence shows what sneering is by showing what Ava does not do.
fact: To sneer means to smile or speak in an unkind way that shows you think someone is not good enough.
fact: A sneer is that unkind, mocking smile, often with one side of the lip lifted.
fact: To sneer at something means to make fun of it as if it were worthless.
fact: «Sneer» is a verb (sneer, sneers, sneered, sneering) and a noun (a sneer, sneers).
fact: Sneering is a kind of disrespect and a sign of bullying, so kind people do not do it.
exercise: «Some girls sneer "Princess Lily" because her hair is neat and her books are tidy.» What does sneer mean here? | Ask Lily to help with homework | Whisper a secret to Lily | Clap for Lily's neat hair | *Make fun of Lily in an unkind way
exercise: Lily is worried about "telling tales", because that is what the boys sneer at. What does sneer at mean? | *Make fun of something as if it were worthless | Smile happily at something | Count something carefully | Hide something under a table
exercise: Which phrase from the lessons describes someone speaking in a mocking, unkind way? | a bright, sunny morning | a soft pillow | *a sneering voice | a happy birthday song
test: «Ava doesn't sneer; she sets up two seed trays instead.» What is Ava doing instead? | Hiding her books | Making fun of the boys | Telling tales about anyone | *Setting up seed trays
test: «At school a kid sneers at Dakota, "Your dad's a criminal, that's well sus".» What does sus mean? | *Dodgy, or not to be trusted | Clean and tidy | Loud and noisy | Happy and cheerful
exam: Which word means a mocking, unkind smile that shows someone thinks another is not good enough? | whisper | kindness | hug | *sneer
